\chapter{Stress-Testing \& Validation Protocols}
\label{chap:stress_testing}

\section{Overview}

Stress-testing evaluates the resilience, stability, and boundedness of the
CC-MSSC v1.0 architecture under extreme forcing conditions. While the Master
Evolution Equation and Lyapunov analysis guarantee theoretical stability,
stress-testing provides empirical confirmation across astrophysical,
structural, metabolic, continuity, and computational domains.

This chapter formalizes the four stress-testing vectors, the forcing regimes,
the validation metrics, and the results demonstrating that CC-MSSC v1.0
remains stable under all tested conditions.

\section{Stress-Testing Vectors}

Stress-testing is organized into four forcing vectors:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Vector 1: Astrophysical Chaos Forcing} — high-amplitude,
    high-frequency entropy injection.
    \item \textbf{Vector 2: Structural Cascade Failure} — progressive
    degradation of structural ontology variables.
    \item \textbf{Vector 3: Load \& Latency Stress} — computational and
    physiological overload scenarios.
    \item \textbf{Vector 4: Adversarial Security Forcing} — hostile perturbation
    vectors designed to destabilize UFSL or continuity identity.
\end{enumerate}

Each vector is designed to push the system toward instability while verifying
that global boundedness is preserved.

